# termiHub curated plugin-index signing key (#3716).
#
# TERMIHUB-PLUGIN-INDEX-KEY-PLACEHOLDER
#
# This file is a PLACEHOLDER: no real signing key has been generated yet. While it
# contains no PUBLIC KEY block, the desktop cannot verify the plugin index, so it
# still loads the default index but labels it "signature not checked" in Browse
# Plugins (the feature keeps working; nothing is reported as verified). This key is
# SEPARATE from the agent update signing key.
#
# The maintainer replaces this file by running (once):
#
#   ./scripts/internal/setup-plugin-index-signing-key.sh
#
# which generates an ed25519 keypair, signs plugins/index.json into
# plugins/index.json.sig, stores the private key ONLY as the
# PLUGIN_INDEX_SIGNING_KEY GitHub Actions secret, and rewrites this file with the
# public key in PEM (SubjectPublicKeyInfo) form. From then on the default index is
# only accepted with a valid signature. See docs/contributing.md ->
# "Plugin index signing key".
